            "Valve Cover Gasket Leaks: The rubber or cork gasket hardens and leaks oil down the side of the engine, often coating the exhaust manifold and causing a burning oil smell.",
            "Coolant Flange Cracking: The plastic coolant neck on the side of the cylinder head becomes brittle from heat and eventually cracks, causing slow coolant loss.",
