        timingType: "Belt (Toothed timing belt driving the single overhead camshaft. Extremely reliable and robust. Also drives the water pump)", injectionType: "KE3-Jetronic (Bosch Continuous Injection System with lambda regulation. An archaic, entirely mechanical fuel distributor with minor electronic trim adjustments)", engineLifespan: "500,000+ km (The legendary Audi inline-5. The cast iron block is immortal, and the 10V head is under no stress. The engine will literally outlast the universe; it is only the surrounding KE-Jetronic fuel system that ages poorly)", turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (No turbocharger. Provides a highly linear, smooth power delivery accompanied by the iconic 5-cylinder warble)", ecuType: "Bosch KE3-Jetronic (Primitive analog management. Diagnostics rely primarily on mechanical pressure gauges rather than modern OBD scanners)", euroStandard: "Euro 1 / Euro 2", maxPowerStockInternals: "400+ hp (The AAR bottom end is legendary. With a turbo conversion and modern EFI, these blocks easily hold massive power, serving as the basis for many budget S2 clones)",
        fuelConsumption: { city: "12.0 - 13.5 L/100km", highway: "7.5 - 8.5 L/100km", mixed: "9.5 - 10.5 L/100km", sporty: "14.5+ L/100km" },
        oilSpecification: "VW 502.00 10W-40 Synthetic Blend",
        commonIssues: [ 
            "Torn Intake Rubber Boot ('Turtle Neck'): The massive rubber boot sitting on top of the mechanical air flow meter plate cracks with age. This causes catastrophic unmetered air leaks, preventing the engine from running or idling.",
            "Idle Stabilizer Valve (ISV): The ISV clogs with oil vapor, causing the engine to surge wildly between 800 and 1500 RPM, or stall entirely when coming to a stop.",
            "Warm Start Issues (Fuel Accumulator): The fuel accumulator loses spring tension, bleeding off system pressure when the car is turned off. Causes 5-10 second cranking times when the engine is warm.",
            "Leaking Injector O-Rings: The rubber seals around the brass mechanical injectors harden, causing localized vacuum leaks at each cylinder.",
            "Vacuum Pump Tapping (Brake Booster): The mechanically driven vacuum pump pushrod wears out, causing a loud, rhythmic tapping noise at idle that is often misdiagnosed as bad lifters.",
            "Distributor Hall Sender Failure: The sensor inside the distributor fails due to heat, causing sudden stalling."
        ],
        vulnerabilities: [ 
            "KE-Jetronic Contamination - If rust or debris enters the mechanical fuel distributor, the incredibly fine internal slits will clog. The car will misfire or run on 4 cylinders. Rebuilding a 5-cylinder fuel distributor is highly specialized and expensive.",
            "Vacuum Leak Stranding - Because KE-Jetronic relies on engine vacuum physically lifting an airflow plate to inject fuel, a large tear in a vacuum line or the intake boot means the car simply will not start. Period.",
            "Timing Belt Failure - Although robust, ignoring the interval will snap the belt and bend the 10 valves.",
            "Heater Core Failure - Standard C4 vulnerability. The matrix bursts, leaking hot coolant.",
            "Exhaust Manifold Cracking - The cast iron exhaust manifold is prone to cracking near the collector, causing a ticking exhaust leak sound on cold starts."
        ],
