        timingType: "Belt (Toothed timing belt driving the camshaft and VP37 injection pump. Highly reliable. The lower crankshaft sprocket wobble issue is slightly improved over the early 1Z, but still requires strict monitoring and replacement during belt jobs)", injectionType: "Direct Injection (Bosch VP37 Electronic Rotary Distributor Pump. Mechanical injection with electronic quantity control. Indestructible but sensitive to air leaks)", engineLifespan: "500,000+ km (The AHU is a slight evolution of the 1Z. The cast-iron block and basic 8V head are immortal. It is common to see these engines hit half a million kilometers with basic maintenance)", turboType: "Wastegate Turbocharger (Garrett T15 or KKK K03. Very simple, robust, but inherently laggy compared to later VNT turbos)", ecuType: "Bosch MSA15 (A 16-bit ECU upgrade over the 1Z's 8-bit. Diagnostic capabilities are slightly better, though tuning often still requires socketing the ECU chips)", euroStandard: "Euro 2", maxPowerStockInternals: "150+ hp (The block is heavily over-engineered, but the factory wastegate turbo and small .184mm injector nozzles severely limit tuning potential without hardware upgrades)",
