        timingType: "Belt & Chain (The primary drive is a massive toothed timing belt spanning the front of the block. Short internal chains link the exhaust to the intake camshafts. Extremely complex, labor-intensive, and critical to replace every 90k km)", injectionType: "Multi-Point Injection (Bosch Motronic sequential port fuel injection. Highly reliable, no carbon buildup issues)", engineLifespan: "350,000+ km (The all-aluminum V8 block is highly durable. The engine's lifespan is almost entirely dictated by the owner's willingness to pay for severe oil leak repairs and incredibly expensive timing belt services)", turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (No turbocharger. Relies on massive displacement and a high-flowing 32-valve head design for smooth, linear power delivery)", ecuType: "Bosch Motronic (A robust, albeit somewhat primitive, dual-bank engine management system. Cannot easily be tuned)", euroStandard: "Euro 2", maxPowerStockInternals: "350+ hp (The block is strong, but extracting significant power from a naturally aspirated 32V V8 is incredibly expensive and difficult without forced induction)",
