        timingType: "Belt & Chain (Toothed timing belt drives the exhaust camshaft; a hydraulic tensioner-driven chain at the rear of the head links the two cams. The chain tensioner is a frequent failure point)", injectionType: "Multi-Point Injection (MPI - Bosch Motronic M3.8.2. Features the highly desirable 'Big Port' head design, which is a favorite for high-horsepower builds due to superior airflow)", engineLifespan: "350,000+ km (The AEB is an absolute tank. It features forged connecting rods from the factory and an external water pump setup. With proper oil changes to prevent sludge, it is nearly indestructible)", turboType: "Single Turbocharger (KKK K03. Small, fast-spooling, but limited in top-end flow)", ecuType: "Bosch Motronic M3.8.2 (Narrowband oxygen sensor control. Tuning requires physical EPROM chip replacement/soldering)", euroStandard: "Euro 2", maxPowerStockInternals: "450+ hp (The AEB is legendary because of its 20mm wrist pins and forged rods. The block and crank can handle massive boost, provided the fueling is upgraded)",
