            drivingExperience: "The 150hp ARK in the A6 C5 is a smooth, refined highway cruiser. Thanks to the fast-spooling K03 turbo, power delivery is exceptionally linear, making it feel capable around town despite the heavy chassis. It retains the older cable-driven throttle, which gives it a slightly more direct mechanical feel compared to the later DBW engines.",
            mechanicVerdict: "The ARK is an excellent, highly tuneable engine. It is simpler than the later AWT (no VVT tensioner, no secondary air injection) but requires physical chip tuning. You MUST use synthetic oil and stick to strict 8k-10k km intervals to prevent oil sludge from killing the engine. Upgrade the oil filter size, fix the fragile PCV system, and it will be an incredibly loyal daily driver.",
